import GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.MpcBalancedRelativeSpan

/-!
# The four coordinate spans of the balanced relative shift

The finite source of `MpcBalancedRelativeSpan` is a direct product of four constrained
coordinate groups.  This file splits its shift range into the four literal coordinate
ranges.  The `A`, `B`, and `D` coordinates range over the relative depth layer; the `C`
coordinate ranges over its character-neutral subgroup.

The result is an exact reformulation of the W209 target-specific range condition, not a
surjectivity claim.  The four coordinate formulas identify the remaining finite spanning
problem with one square-and-two-brackets row and three single-bracket rows.
-/

namespace GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.MpcBalancedCoordinateSpan

noncomputable section

open GQ2 GQ2.Dyadic Multiplicative
